Claude Code subagent definitions go here, and stay the exception rather than the rule.

Unlike skills, subagents have no cross-vendor standard — the Agent Skills spec covers
skills only — so anything written here works in Claude Code and nowhere else. When a
task could be expressed either way, write a skill in .agents/skills/ instead. A
subagent earns its place when it needs what a skill can't give it — its own tool
allowlist, or a context window isolated from the main conversation — the way
`client-reviewer.md` restricts itself to read-only tools plus `ReportFindings` for a
review that shouldn't also carry edit access.
